### Banking Transaction System - sample requests
### Open in IntelliJ IDEA or VS Code (REST Client extension) and click "Send Request".
### Run 1 (or 2), copy the "token" from the response into @token below, then run the rest.

@base = http://localhost:8080/api
@token = paste-token-here

### 1. Sign up as a customer (also opens a savings account and returns a token)
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Anil Katroth", "email": "anil@example.com", "phone": "9652336856",
  "username": "anil", "password": "Secret123" }

### 2. Log in
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "anil", "password": "Secret123" }

### 3. My profile and accounts (note your accountNumber, e.g. 100000000001)
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Open a second (current) account
POST {{base}}/me/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "accountType": "CURRENT" }

### 5. Deposit
POST {{base}}/accounts/100000000001/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 5000.00, "description": "Salary" }

### 6. Check who owns the receiving account before sending
GET {{base}}/accounts/100000000002/holder
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Transfer (send twice: the second call returns the same result, money moves once)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromAccountNumber": "100000000001", "toAccountNumber": "100000000002",
  "amount": 1200.00, "referenceNo": "RENT-OCT-2026", "description": "October rent" }

### 8. Withdraw more than the balance -> 422 Insufficient funds
POST {{base}}/accounts/100000000002/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 99999.00 }

### 9. Recent activity
GET {{base}}/accounts/100000000001/transactions?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Statement for a date range
GET {{base}}/accounts/100000000001/statement?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Admin: log in, then put this token in @token to call the admin endpoints
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "Admin@123" }

### 12. Admin: totals
GET {{base}}/admin/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Admin: all customers with accounts
GET {{base}}/admin/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. Admin: freeze an account
PATCH {{base}}/accounts/100000000002/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "FROZEN" }
